	<div class="intraNav" id="51683" data-intranav="Overview of Member Platforms"></div><section class="">
	<div class="text-container">
		
				<div class="container">
					<div class="row">
						<div class="col-xl-8 offset-xl-2">
							
								<h2>Overview of Member Platforms</h2>
							
							
							
							<p><!--StartFragment -->The following admission platforms are available to ECC members as well as trading participants and customers of EEX<!--EndFragment -->:</p>
<h3>ECC</h3><table class="table"> 	<thead class="thead-dark"> 		<tr> 			<th scope="col">Platform</th> 			<th scope="col">Functionalities</th> 		</tr> 	</thead> 	<tbody> 		<tr> 			<td><a href="https://www.ecc.de/en/access/member-platforms#52118" target="_blank">Member Area</a></td> 			<td> 			<ul class="content-list"> 				<li>ECC Reports (trading, payment, invoice reports) and limit management​</li> 			</ul> 			</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td><a href="https://production.eurexclearing.com:8443/C7_GUI/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">C7 GUI</a></td> 			<td> 			<ul class="content-list"> 				<li>Position- and Transactionmanagement​</li> 			</ul> 			</td> 		</tr> 	</tbody> </table><h3>ECC and EEX</h3><table class="table"> 	<thead class="thead-dark"> 		<tr> 			<th scope="col">Platform</th> 			<th scope="col">Functionalities</th> 		</tr> 	</thead> 	<tbody> 		<tr> 			<td><a href="https://customerportal.eex.com/login.jsp" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Customer Portal</a></td> 			<td> 			<ul class="content-list"> 				<li>Request and monitor changes on company level: product extensions, change of company data and terminations​</li> 			</ul> 			</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td><a href="https://membersection.deutsche-boerse.com/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Member Section</a></td> 			<td> 			<ul class="content-list"> 				<li>Management of Central Coordinators, Deputies & Member Section Users </li> 				<li>ECC Specific: Technical Infrastructure (C7 GUI Certificates, C7 FIXML, Leased Lines, Common Report Engine (CRE))​</li> 				<li>EEX Specific: Trader Admission and Termination, Technical Infrastructure (ETI Session, T7 GUI Certificates, Common Upload Engine (CUE), Common Report Engine (CRE)), Short Codes & Algo ID Uploads, User ID Maintenance</li> 			</ul> 			</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td><a href="https://www.nehs-zulassung.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">nEHS Admission Platform</a></td> 			<td> 			<ul class="content-list"> 				<li>Admission platform for German national Emission certificates (nEHS)​</li> 			</ul> 			</td> 		</tr> 	</tbody> </table><h3>EEX</h3><table class="table"> 	<thead class="thead-dark"> 		<tr> 			<th scope="col">Platform</th> 			<th scope="col">Functionalities</th> 		</tr> 	</thead> 	<tbody> 		<tr> 			<td><a href="https://backoffice-members.powernext.com/index.php?:nav=auth::login" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">EEX Backoffice</a></td> 			<td> 			<ul class="content-list"> 				<li>For Gas only: invoices and trade reports​</li> 			</ul> 			</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td><a href="https://t7gui.production.eurex.com/xeee/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Eurex T7 GUI Trading System</a></td> 			<td> 			<ul class="content-list"> 				<li>Order book management, trade execution, real-time market data, supports automated trading, market making activity support, setup of user IDs / view user permissions and maintain transaction size limits​</li> 			</ul> 			</td> 		</tr> 	</tbody> </table><p>Please find more information on connectivity options on the <a href="https://www.eex.com/en/trading-resources/technical-information/frontends" target="_blank">EEX website</a>.</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				
	</div>
</section><div class="intraNav" id="52142" data-intranav="Central Coordinator"></div><section class="mt-xl-3 mt-md-2 mt-1">
	<div class="text-container">
		
				<div class="container">
					<div class="row">
						<div class="col-xl-8 offset-xl-2">
							
								<h2>Central Coordinator</h2>
							
							
							
							<p>The Central Coordinator is the member’s representative and is appointed as the main contact person for exchange (concerning EEX Membership) and ECC clearing related membership matters. Central Coordinators can also appoint deputies.  </p>
<p>The Central Coordinator (and any Deputy Central Coordinator) is responsible for the following matters: </p><ol> 	<li>Responsibility for the internal distribution of all EEX, EEX AG and/or ECC AG information; </li> 	<li>Authorization to represent and make declarations on behalf of the member towards EEX, EEX AG and/or ECC AG in all exchange and clearing membership related matters; and  </li> 	<li>Administrative access to the Member Section and the Customer Portal, and the user accounts therein.</li> </ol><h3>How to become a Central Coordinator</h3>
<p>A Central Coordinator is appointed during a member’s admission process. If you are an existing member and have not yet appointed a Central Coordinator, please fill in and sign the form below, and send it by email to <a href="mailto:memberreadiness@ecc.de" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">memberreadiness@ecc.de</a>.</p>
<p>On receiving your completed form, the Member Section Support Team (<a href="mailto:member.section@deutsche-boerse.com" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">member.section@deutsche-boerse.com</a>) will send you an email with your login credentials and detailed instructions on how to access the Member Section. From that point on Central Coordinators will be able to manage their own and their deputies' contact details directly in the Member Section. </p>
<p>Central Coordinators and deputies will also receive an email with detailed instructions on how to access the Customer Portal. You do not need to request your Customer Portal access separately.</p>
<hr>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				
	</div>
</section>


